        "id": 5054,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2011-08-12T11:48:15.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Now what I mean by this is Villians that can played against with maybe one or two Heroes, so people who can’t get a hold of somebody but they also aren’t in the mood to keep up with four different heroes. Also, if there are two of these weaker Villians that they can be fought at the same time if there are more heroes able to do battle against them. Together they’ll probably be very difficult to beat since they will each have their own turn which will mean two Villian cards will be drawn each round. So two villians, each with their own twenty-five card deck, that can be fought seperately with one or two Heroes, or fought together with the three to five heroes. Anyone else thinking that this coudl lead to an interesting development?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:34:36.680Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
